course: dictionary
lesson: 9808
title: One word, two jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words can be a thing or an action. Swan is one of them. The words around it tell you which job it is doing. «Swans get tangled in old fishing line» names the animals, so swan is a noun here, meaning a bird.
explain: Look for clues about the bird. In «It's a swan, bro, and it's black», the word black describes the bird, so swan means a large water bird, usually white, with a long curved neck. A black swan is a bird that is not white, which shows the usual colour is white.
explain: Now read this: «He swanned off to the beach while we cleaned the kitchen.» Swanned has the word off after it, and the sentence shows that one person is relaxed while others work. Here swan is a verb, and it means to go somewhere in a carefree way. This is informal British English, so you will hear it in speech more than in books.
explain: To check, swap in your meaning. Does «He went off to the beach in a carefree way while we cleaned the kitchen» still make sense? It does, so you have the right meaning. The feeling matters too: the speaker is annoyed.
fact: A swan is a large water bird, usually white, with a long curved neck.
fact: Swans live on rivers and lakes. A young swan is a cygnet, a male is a cob, and a female is a pen.
fact: As a verb, swan is informal and British. «Swanning off» means going somewhere relaxed while others are working.
fact: The speaker in «swanning off» is often annoyed, not just describing a trip.
fact: In stories like «The Ugly Duckling», the swan stands for beauty and grace.
exercise: «Swans get tangled in old fishing line.» In this sentence, is swan a noun or a verb? | A verb, meaning to go off relaxed | A verb, meaning to swim fast | An adjective, meaning white | *A noun, meaning a bird
exercise: What is a young swan called? | Cob | *Cygnet | Nest | Pen
exercise: Jack says, «He just swanned off and left us to do the washing up.» What does swanned off suggest? | Ran away fast | *Went off relaxed while others worked | Was happy to help with the work | Went off to look for a swan
test: Which best describes the swan in «It's a swan, bro, and it's black»? | A young bird | A tangled fishing line | *A large water bird, usually white | A relaxed, carefree way of going
test: Which sentence uses swan as a verb? | «A swan has a long curved neck.» | *«He swanned off to the beach while we cleaned the kitchen.» | «Swans get tangled in old fishing line.» | «Geese and swans are not being mean.»
exam: Which best sums up the swan in «The Ugly Duckling»? | Fear | Speed | *Beauty and grace | Mischief
